% ============================================================================
% solfege-alt-name.query.adj — a worked recall over the music
% solfege-alt-name library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what's another way to
% spell 'do'?": it states no music fact of its own — it only `import`s the
% grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?`
% against the `solfege_alt_name` rows and returns the alternate + the
% table's source/locator/trust. A syllable the cited span gives no
% alternate for (e.g. "mi") abstains honestly — the engine never invents
% one.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli solfege-alt-name.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "solfege-alt-name.adj"

? solfege_alt_name(do, $Alt)          % expect doh
? solfege_alt_name($Syllable, si)      % expect ti
? solfege_alt_name(mi, $Alt)           % expect abstain — mi's own cited span states no alternate
